[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## How this table was derived
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Public entry points (complete set)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/include/driver.h` exports exactly one entry point, and it is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m simultaneously the highest- and lowest-level one — there is no convenience
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m wrapper layered over a lower-level API:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m void driver(double f);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is therefore no "call the low-level API directly" variant to add; every
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m row below drives `driver` itself.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Runtime options / modes / flags
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Grep of the C source for option state: **none exist**. There is no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `#ifdef` in `driver.c` or `driver.h`, no flag parameter, no global/`static`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m configuration variable, no setter, no environment lookup, no locale call.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `translation/Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so there is no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m compile-time axis either. The single configuration axis is therefore the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **shape of the one input value**.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Input shapes the code actually distinguishes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `driver` funnels its argument into three conversions, and it is those
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m conversions' branches that the input shape selects:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m raw_double_t u = {.f = f};              /* type-punned reinterpretation  */
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m printf("%llx %a %.4f\n", u.x, f, f);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `%llx` — branches on the raw 64-bit pattern: leading-zero suppression means
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the field width varies from 1 to 16 hex digits, and the all-zero pattern is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   special (must still emit one `0`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `%a` (glibc `__printf_fphex`) — branches on: the sign bit; whether the biased
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   exponent field is `0` (leading digit `0`, no renormalisation), `0x7ff`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`inf`/`nan` names, numeric path skipped entirely), `>= 1023` (`p+`) or
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `< 1023` (`p-`); and whether the 52-bit mantissa is zero (radix point and all
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   13 digits suppressed) or has trailing zero nibbles (trailing-zero trimming).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `%.4f` (glibc `__printf_fp`) — branches on: sign; non-finite names; whether
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the magnitude rounds to `0.0000`; whether the integer part is `0` (leading
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `0.`) or many digits (up to 309 for `DBL_MAX`); and the round-half-to-even
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   decision at the 4th fractional digit, including carry propagation across the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   radix point.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The rows below are the cross-product of {sign} × {exponent-field class} ×
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m {mantissa shape} × {`%.4f` magnitude class}, pruned to the combinations the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m actually treats differently. Each row is exercised in `tests/differential.rs`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m with **many randomized inputs drawn from that row's class using a fixed seed**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (SplitMix64, seed `0x2545F4914F6CDD1D`), never a single hand-picked value, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m compared byte-for-byte between the C `.so` and the Rust `.so`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
